%% F3--F5: Summary (details in Appendix B)
%% ============================================================

\subsection{F3--F5: Factorial Ablation (Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_factorial})}
\label{sec:f3f5_summary}

Trained $\dt$-embedding and multi-rate data exposure are \emph{jointly necessary} for CIVO. Neither factor alone triggers pathological overestimation: trained embedding without multi-rate exposure (008a, NVE $= 0.93\times$) and multi-rate exposure without embedding (008f, NVE $= 0.97\times$) both remain well below the $1.5\times$ diagnostic threshold, while frozen embedding under full exposure (015b) peaks near the diagnostic threshold ($1.45\times$ at 55K) but retreats to $0.55\times$ by 105K, confirming frozen embedding prevents the sustained escalation characteristic of CIVO (Figure~\ref{fig:factorial_grid}). Degradation scales monotonically with $\dt$ ($-47\%$ at $\dt{=}2$, $-81\%$ at $\dt{=}4$; Figure~\ref{fig:dt_amplification}).

